# ADAMAS reference database (part A: classical electronics). One reference per line, pipe-separated:
# key | authors | year | title | venue | locator | tags | status
# status: V = bibliographic details confirmed against an online source while this repo was built (September 2026)
#         K = entered from literature knowledge; run tools/verify_refs.py to confirm against Crossref before citing in a paper
# tags: mat (materials), waf (wafers and growth), si (silicon baseline), dop (doping, surfaces, processing),
#       dev (devices and circuits), thm (thermal), nv (NV physics), sens (sensing), fab (NV fabrication),
#       qc (quantum computing), net (photonics and networks), ind (industry news), edu (teaching)
